    <title>Coffee: History and Spread</title>
    <content>
<![CDATA[
<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM 'http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd'>
<en-note>
<h2>History of coffee</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Wild coffee plants are thought to be native to an Ethiopian plateau region (Kefa/Kaffa).</li>
  <li>Coffee was cultivated in Yemen and spread to the wider world.</li>
  <li>Coffeehouses appeared in Mecca in the 15th century and later in Istanbul.</li>
</ul>
<p>References: <a href="https://www.britannica.com/topic/history-of-coffee">Britannica: History of coffee</a>; <a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/magazine-22190802">BBC: Coffee and qahwa</a></p>
